  // be copied onto a recruited instance only once, at recruitment (see the
  // spread in recruitWarrior), exactly like w.defaultSkills just below used
  // to be before V-DEFAULTSKILLSYNC. An admin granting a fighter TYPE access
  // to an item after some of that type were already recruited (reported: a
  // Blood Knight checked for Lance/Barding in Blood Dragons) left every
  // already-recruited copy stuck on the OLD list forever, with no visible
  // error — warriorBandAllowed simply never saw the new name. There is no
  // player-facing way to set this independently of the template, so it's
  // always safe to mirror it fresh on every load, the same way rules/
  // ruleNames just above already do.
  if(Array.isArray(w.equipmentAccess))x.equipmentAccess=w.equipmentAccess.slice();
  if(w.equipmentAccessGroups!==undefined)x.equipmentAccessGroups=w.equipmentAccessGroups==='ALL'?'ALL':(Array.isArray(w.equipmentAccessGroups)?w.equipmentAccessGroups.slice():[]);
  if(!Array.isArray(x.advancements))x.advancements=[];if(!Array.isArray(x.skills))x.skills=[];
  // V-DEFAULTSKILLSYNC: w.defaultSkills used to be applied ONLY at
  // recruitment time (addFighter/recruitFreeExplorationWarrior bake it into
  // the fresh fighter's skills array once, on creation) — a fighter already
  // recruited before its template's default skills were set/changed (an
